touch .env
# The URL where your devil-api backend is running
PRIVATE_DEVIL_API_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"

# The authorization key required by devil-api
PRIVATE_DEVIL_API_KEY="your_secure_api_key_here"

# Optional: Set to "true" if you are developing locally without SSL/HTTPS
ALLOW_INSECURE_BACKEND="true"
//-front end-/-back end-//
PRIVATE_DEVIL_API_URL="[http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000)"
PRIVATE_DEVIL_API_KEY="your_secure_hex_token"
ALLOW_INSECURE_BACKEND="false"
# Start backend service
cd devil-api
pm2 start "venv/bin/uvicorn main:app --port 8000" --name "devil-backend"

# Start frontend service
cd ../devil-web
npm run build
pm2 start node --name "devil-frontend" -- build/index.js

# Persist processes across system reboots
pm2 save
pm2 startup

---

### Key Reasons to Update This Right Now:
* **API Documentation:** It lists exactly what variables go into your `.env` files so you don't forget them if your server crashes.
* **Process Management:** It saves the exact `pm2` command strings needed to bring the site back up after updates. 
* **Deployment Context:** If you share the repository link with peers or team members, they will instantly understand how the frontend interface talks to the socket engine backend.
